# platform.pico_epaper_b.display

The physical display provider for the Waveshare Pico-ePaper-2.66-B carrier.
It owns the tri-color initialization, both controller RAM planes, geometry,
and fixed GPIO/SPI wiring, then registers the controller as mm.display.

Packed image writes remain black and white in this stage. They explicitly
clear the red plane, while clear(red) exercises a uniform red frame. Arbitrary
three-color image composition requires a future multi-plane display contract.
